WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.910
Read this.

2
00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:03.330
"Nina's tea had gone cold.

3
00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:05.150
Her coat was still on.

4
00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:07.250
She kept looking at the window.

5
00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:10.010
" The writer never tells
you how Nina feels.

6
00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:12.070
Not one word about it.

7
00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:14.510
Yet you may feel sure you know.

8
00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:17.710
So how can you know something
a writer never wrote?

9
00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:19.710
And is it just a guess?

10
00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:24.050
In this mission, you'll learn
three ways to read: skimming,

11
00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:25.660
scanning and close reading.

12
00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:29.650
You'll read between the lines,
and back up what you find.

13
00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:33.550
And you'll spot the big idea
a story keeps coming back to.

14
00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:37.860
Your mission: work out how you
can know what is never said.
